  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Ford Motor recorded $619M in contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Ford Motor has 16,399 awards this fiscal year so far, with an average award size of $37.7K. Ford Motor obligations are up 30.5% year over year. Ford Motor obligations by fiscal year show variability: FY21 $503M, FY22 $688M, FY23 $307M, FY24 $580M, FY25 $474M, and FY26 $619M. Ford Motor sales to the federal government concentrate heavily in a single buyer and a single market. The General Services Administration obligated $619M to Ford Motor. Automobile Manufacturing is the largest NAICS market for Ford Motor at $619M. The current-year totals are partial, covering the fiscal year to date. The dataset notes that figures are contract obligations except award-value figures in the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables, which are total contract values. This summary focuses on obligations reported through FY2026 to date.",
